      "file": "src/pcre2_fuzzsupport.c",
      "function": "LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput",
      "line": 134,
      "code": "code = pcre2_compile((PCRE2_SPTR)data, (PCRE2_SIZE)size, compile_options,\n  &errorcode, &erroroffset, NULL);",
      "note": "The harness forwards the exact staged witness bytes into the PCRE2 compiler. Compilation succeeds in the reproduced run because execution later reaches `pcre2_match_8` and the crashing `match()` epilogue.",
      "oracle_kind": "gt_parser_checkpoint",
      "kind": "parser_admitted"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/pcre2_compile.c",
      "function": "parse_regex",
      "line": 3272,
      "code": "if ((options & PCRE2_NO_AUTO_CAPTURE) == 0)\n  {\n  cb->bracount++;\n  *parsed_pattern++ = META_CAPTURE | cb->bracount;\n  }\nelse *parsed_pattern++ = META_NOCAPTURE;",
      "note": "When `parse_regex` handles the witness's only explicit `(`, it either increments `cb->bracount` once or emits `META_NOCAPTURE` depending on `PCRE2_NO_AUTO_CAPTURE`. This is the first project-code site that materializes the small capture-count state later stored in `re->top_bracket`.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/pcre2_match.c",
      "function": "match",
      "line": null,
      "code": "memcpy(ovector+2, Fovector, (oveccount - 1) * 2 * sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE));",
      "note": "The result-copy length is derived only from the external `oveccount`, so the harness-fixed 32-pair ovector makes `match()` copy 31 capture pairs before it consults `top_bracket + 1`. For this witness the crashing compiled pattern has `top_bracket <= 1`, so the internal frame provides at most one capture pair and the copy over-reads it. The fix first clamps with `min(top_bracket + 1, oveccount)` before calling `memcpy`.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/pcre2_match.c",
      "function": "match",
      "line": 819,
      "code": "memcpy(ovector+2, Fovector, (oveccount - 1) * 2 * sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE));",
      "note": "The result-copy length is derived only from the external `oveccount`, so the harness-fixed 32-pair ovector makes `match()` copy 31 capture pairs before it consults `top_bracket + 1`. For this witness the crashing compiled pattern has `top_bracket <= 1`, so the internal frame provides at most one capture pair and the copy over-reads it. The fix first clamps with `min(top_bracket + 1, oveccount)` before calling `memcpy`.",
      "kind": "root_cause_line"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/pcre2_match.c",
      "function": "match",
      "line": null,
      "code": "memcpy(ovector+2, Fovector, (oveccount - 1) * 2 * sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE));",
